meta {
  name: Close Month
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/close-month
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "messId": "{{messId}}",
    "adminId": "{{adminMemberId}}",
    "yearMonth": "2026-02"
  }
}

docs {
  # Close Month

  **Requires `SYSTEM_ADMIN` role.**

  Finalises a calendar month by:
  1. Calculating the definitive meal rate
  2. Settling each member's balance
  3. Persisting a `MonthlySnapshot` (status → `CLOSED`)

  Once closed a month **cannot be re-opened**. Any attempt returns HTTP 409.

  ## Responses
  | Code | Meaning |
  |------|---------|
  | 200  | `MonthCloseResponse` with snapshot details |
  | 400  | Validation error (bad yearMonth format, missing fields) |
  | 401  | Missing or invalid token |
  | 403  | Insufficient role (not SYSTEM_ADMIN) |
  | 404  | Mess not found |
  | 409  | Month already closed |
}
